# 04 — THE DESIGN LAW

## SHOW FIRST.

## REVEAL SECOND.

## EXPLAIN WHEN NEEDED.

## LET THE USER DISCOVER.

Never dump the architecture onto the user.

Never use a paragraph where an interaction can communicate the idea better.

Never use a generic card where a spatial object can communicate the concept.

Never use five sentences where three carefully chosen words will work.

Never make the user wonder:

> “What am I supposed to do?”

The interface should answer that visually.

